Here's an example of how you could use this code:

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    String htmlString = "<form id='myForm' title='My Form'><input type='text' name='txtName' value='John Doe'/></form>";
    String[] options = { "utf-8" };

    DOMParser parser = new DOMParser();
    List<HTMLElement> elements = parser.parse(htmlString, options);

    for (HTMLElement element : elements) {
        System.out.println(element.getId());
        System.out.println(element.getTitle());
        System.out.println(element.getCssQuery());
        System.out.println(element.getCharset().getName());

        if (element instanceof TextElement) {
            TextElement textElement = (TextElement) element;
            System.out.println(textElement.getText());
        }

        for (Map.Entry<String, Object> entry : element.attributes.entrySet()) {
            System.out.println(entry.getKey() + ": " + entry.getValue());
        }
    }
}
```

This code will output the ID of each form element, its title, CSS query string, charset name, and text content. It also prints out any attribute values for elements with text content.
